    "data": {
      "id": 2237,
      "hub_id": 2940,
      "guid": "com.somtam.playerlives",
      "name": "Player Lives",
      "slug": "player-lives",
      "teaser": "Die. Revive. Repeat.",
      "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/2940.png",
      "downloads": 7313,
      "favourites_count": 8,
      "description": "<p>In raid lives. When you die you can press a button to revive yourself.</p>\n<p>When you about to get killed, you get put into a critical state where you can crawl around but you can’t use items or guns etc.</p>\n<p>The AI will still shoot at you in this critical state. You need to crawl to safety, then revive.</p>\n<p>On revival, you get 10s of invulnerability where you can stand up and start running to cover.</p>\n<p>While invulnerable, you can’t shoot and you can’t use items etc. You can only run and seek cover.</p>\n<p>So you can’t cheese it by dying, going invul and shoot the AI.</p>\n<p>You can choose how many lives you get per raid.</p>\n<p>Optionally, require a buff from a specific stim in order for the revive to work.</p>\n<p>Or if you want, require a stim to be in the inventory that is consumed to do the revive.</p>\n<p><strong>Optional requirements are AND.</strong> So if you select active buff, AND stim in inventory, you will need both buff and stim to be true before the revive will work.</p>\n<p>Play hardcore, get head eyes, no worries just revive yourself and try again.</p>\n<p>An alternative for those that want to experience tarkov pain, but with the ability to revive in case it goes wrong.</p>\n<p><strong>Press F12 to change the number of lives you get.</strong></p>\n<p>--</p>\n<p>This mod started out as a fork of the revival mod</p>\n",
      "detail_url": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/2237/player-lives",
